# f1 = total
# The inner loop stands under the cleanup of the outer for-of. What it adds up is the answer of `charCodeAt` on what a step handed out: a reader of characters reads its receiver as `word[at]` does, so its
# answer is a read of the loop, the loop reckons with what it reads, its typed turns may begin again, and the sum is asked for a number once in front and goes round unboxed.
